# Every block of a shipped reference that carries an absolute, judged once.
# hash<TAB>prohibition|enforced|bounded<TAB>why
#
# prohibition  assigns a duty to a named authority; contrary execution breaks
#              the duty rather than falsifying the sentence
# enforced     a factual claim whose mechanism is named
# bounded      rewritten to what the artifact supports, so not absolute in force
#
# Editing a block changes its hash and requires a fresh judgement. That is the
# point: the rule this enforces had four hand-audits and each found a different
# subset, because absolutes enter faster than anyone re-reads.

